reason i made this:
- to learn: i'm taking a course and want to implement my knowledge into something that isn't my homework
- possible resume?: obviously the notes will be adjusted to suit that, like sentence casing and making it professional
- hobby: i have not found myself bored with this yet, so hoorah

goal:
- mega application hub; a phone 
- basically a huge application that lets the user do different things if that makes sense

What is implemented already
- Concrete App class that will serve as a parent class for all App subclasses
- Abstract Game class that extends App and implements Playable thats serves as a parent class for all Game subclasses 
- Abstract Utility class that extends App that serves as a parent class for all Utility subclasses
- Input class that takes either an int, double or String, and a String prompt, that will print the prompt into console and respond to the user's input, and also has condition checking for input mismatch
- AppHub class for main method testing
- GameStats class that implements Storable<ArrayList<Integer> saves and loads stats for classes that have stats (aggregation)
- UtilityStorage class that implements Storable<ArrayList<String> saves and loads data for utility objects
- Interface Playable for playable classes
- Interface HasMenu for classes that require a menu
- Interface Storable<E> for classes that have data that can be stored and saved
- NumberGuessingGame class that extends Game and implements HasMenu and Playable(Game)
- Calculator class that extends Utility(App)
- Notes class that extends Utility(App) and implements HasMenu
- ToDoList class that extends Utility(App) and implements HasMenu

